@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@andiToken = {{loginAndi.response.body.data.access_token}}
@budiToken = {{loginBudi.response.body.data.access_token}}
@pengelolaToken = {{loginPengelola.response.body.data.access_token}}
@notificationId = {{listUnread.response.body.data.0.id}}

# Notification API requests (C-A1 to C-A6). Run this file after
# http/bookings.http BK-01 to BK-12 with the worker running, so Andi already
# has notifications. It reuses the same *.bk users as that file.

### Setup: login Andi as peminjam
# @name loginAndi
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "andi.bk@kampus.ac.id", "password": "rahasia123" }

### Setup: login Budi as another peminjam
# @name loginBudi
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "budi.bk@kampus.ac.id", "password": "rahasia123" }

### Setup: login Citra as pengelola
# @name loginPengelola
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "citra.bk@kampus.ac.id", "password": "rahasia123" }

### C-A1 owner sees only their own notifications, newest first → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A1 without a token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications

### C-A2 only unread notifications → 200
# @name listUnread
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?is_read=false
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A2 is_read=true is not part of the contract → 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?is_read=true
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A2 is_read=0 is not a boolean → 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?is_read=0
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A3 unread count → 200 (data.count)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### Setup: Budi's notification id, used by the C-A4 ownership check
# @name listBudi
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{budiToken}}

### C-A4 mark own notification as read → 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A4 marking another user's notification → 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/{{listBudi.response.body.data.0.id}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A4 invalid notification id → 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/bukan-object-id/read
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A5 mark all own notifications as read → 200 (data.updated)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{andiToken}}

### C-A6 pengelola does not see borrowers' notifications → 200, empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{pengelolaToken}}

### C-A6 pengelola unread count stays zero → 200 (data.count = 0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{pengelolaToken}}

### C-A6 pengelola cannot mark a borrower's notification → 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Authorization: Bearer {{pengelolaToken}}
